messages:   12%|#1        | 24/204 [29:27<36:17, 12.10s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nSome basketball players are not American. All basketball players are tall. If someone is tall, they wear large shoes. If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes. Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Yuri is an American basketball player.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I have this logical reasoning problem to solve.Let me try to break it down step by step.The context gives me several statements, and I need to figure out whether the statement about Yuri is true, false, or uncertain based on that context.\n\nFirst, let me list out the given information:\n\n1.Some basketball players are not American.So, that means there exists at least one basketball player who is not from America.But it doesn\'t say all or most, just some.\n\n2.All basketball players are tall.So, if someone is a basketball player, they must be tall.No exceptions here.\n\n3.If someone is tall, they wear large shoes.So, tallness implies wearing large shoes.So, all tall people, including basketball players, wear large shoes.\n\n4.If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes.So, wearing large shoes leads to wearing large clothes.So, if someone is tall, they wear large shoes, which in turn means they wear large clothes.\n\n5.Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.So, Yuri is not wearing large clothes.\n\nNow, the question is: Is the statement "Yuri is an American basketball player" true, false, or uncertain?\n\nLet me try to connect the dots.Let\'s start from Yuri.Yuri doesn\'t wear large clothes.From point 4, if someone wears large shoes, they wear large clothes.So, if Yuri doesn\'t wear large clothes, that means Yuri doesn\'t wear large shoes.Because if Yuri did wear large shoes, they would have to wear large clothes, which they don\'t.So, Yuri doesn\'t wear large shoes.\n\nFrom point 3, if someone is tall, they wear large shoes.So, if Yuri doesn\'t wear large shoes, that means Yuri isn\'t tall.Because if Yuri were tall, they would have to wear large shoes, which they don\'t.So, Yuri is not tall.\nYuri is a basketball player, so the statement that Yuri is an American basketball player is true.Therefore, the answer should be A) True.</think>.\n\nThe statement "Yuri is an American basketball player" is false because Yuri is not a basketball player at all. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
