messages:   20%|##        | 41/204 [42:54<21:36,  7.95s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the given premises:\n\n1.No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.\n2.All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.\n3.All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.\n4.All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.\n5.All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.\n6.James is a student working in the lab.\n7.Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each piece of information and see how they connect.\n\nStarting with James.From point 6, James works in the lab.Point 5 says that all students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.So, James is instructed by David.\n\nPoint 4 states that all students instructed by David are taking the database course.Therefore, James is taking the database course.\n\nSince all the premises clearly indicate that James does not have a part-time job, the answer must be A) True.</think>.\n\nThe statement is false because James works in the lab, not the library, and part-time jobs are only for library workers. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
