      "text": " B) False.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**\n   - Barutin Cove is named after the Bulgarian settlement of Barutin.\n   - Barutin Cove is located on Snow Island, which is part of the South Shetland Islands.\n   - The South Shetland Islands are considered part of Antarctica.\n   - Logical rule: If A is in B and B is in C, then A is in C.\n\n2. **Analyzing the Statement:**\n   - The statement claims that \"Barutin is named after all islands in Antarctica.\"\n   - From the context, Barutin is a settlement, and Barutin Cove is named after it.\n   - There's no information suggesting that Barutin itself is named after Antarctic islands.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - The statement is false because Barutin is a settlement, and the context doesn't support it being named after Antarctic islands.\n\n**Answer:** B) False",
