e \u2192 hardcover book.)\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n- From Premise 3 and 1: Streaming services are digital, so they cannot be analog.\n- From Premise 2: Printed text is analog, so it cannot be digital.\n- If 1984 were a streaming service (Premise 5), it would be a hardcover book (Premise 4), which is printed text (analog). But this contradicts Premise 1 because streaming services are digital, not analog.\n- Therefore, 1984 cannot be a streaming service.\n- Since 1984 is not a streaming service, Premise 5 does not apply, and we have no information linking 1984 to being a hardcover book or printed text.\n- Without additional information, we cannot determine if 1984 is printed text.\n\n**Conclusion:** The statement \"1984 is printed text\" is uncertain.\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n\\boxed{C}",
