messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nBadults is a British Sitcom series, starring members of Pappy\'s. Badults piloted in July 2013 on BBC Three. The Working title "The Secret Dude Society" was used for Badults. Andrew Collins was the script editor for Badults\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Andrew Collins was the script editor for a series with the working title "The Secret Dude Society".\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.Let me read through the context again carefully.\n\nThe context says that Badults is a British Sitcom series, starring members of Pappy\'s.It piloted in July 2013 on BBC Three.The working title was "The Secret Dude Society" for Badults.Andrew Collins was the script editor for Badults.\n\nThe question is asking if the statement "Andrew Collins was the script editor for a series with the working title \'The Secret Dude Society\'" is true, false, or uncertain.\n\nSo, breaking it down, the series in question is Badults, which had the working title "The Secret Dude Society."Andrew Collins was the script editor for Badults.Therefore, since Badults is the series with that working title, and Andrew Collins was the script editor for Badults, the statement should be true.\n\nGo ahead, as it\'s clear that there\'s confusion.The working title is not for Badults, and Andrew wasn\'t the script editor for Badults.So no, he wasn\'t the script editor for the series that had that working title.So the statement is false.\n\nI do see conflicting information here.The context doesn\'t directly link Andrew Collins to Badults as the script editor and doesn\'t mention the working title for Badults.So there\'s uncertainty and contradiction.</think>.\n\nThe statement is true because Andrew Collins was the script editor for Badults, which had the working title "The Secret Dude Society.". Therefore, my final option is: ']]
