 ∧ false) ∨ (false ∧ true) → false ∨ false → false.\n\nSo, the implication is false → (C ∨ D) → (true ∨ false) → true. Thus, the implication is false.\n\nCase 2: A false, B true.\n\nFrom premise 3: B → ¬C, so C is false.\n\nFrom premise 2: P ∨ D.\n\nSince C is false, from premise 1, P must be false.\n\nTherefore, D must be true (from premise 2: P ∨ D).\n\nFrom premise 4: D → B, which is true because B is true.\n\nHence, in this case, C is false, D is true.\n\nNow, the antecedent is (A ∧ B) ∨ (¬A ∧ ¬B) → (false ∧ true) ∨ (true ∧ false) → false ∨ false → false.\n\nSo, the implication is false → (C ∨ D) → (false ∨ true) → true. Therefore, the implication is false.\n\nCase 3: A false, B false.\n\nFrom premise 4: D → B. Since B is false, D must be false.\n\nFrom premise 2: P ∨ D. Since D is false, P must be true.\n\nFrom premise 1: P → C, so C is true.\n\nThus, in this case, C is true, D is false.\n\nNow, the antecedent is (A ∧ B) ∨ (¬A ∧ ¬B) → (false ∧ false) ∨ (true ∧ true) → false ∨ true → true.\n\nThe consequent is (C ∨ D) → (true ∨ false) → true.\n\nTherefore, the implication is true → true, which is true.\n\nTherefore, in all possible cases, the implication is invalid.\n\nHence, the statement is false.\n\n</think>.\n\nThe statement is true based on the given premises. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 52%|#####1    | 106/204 [2:07:42<1:46:16, 65.06s/it]
