rtain.\n\nWait, I think I\'m overcomplicating this.Let me try to make a decision.\n\nThe key points are:\n\n- Rock must be either a fly or a bird.\n- If Rock is a bird, it has wings, so the statement is true.\n- If Rock is a fly, we know it has wings because flies can fly.\n- Therefore, the statement is certain because we do know whether Rock is a bird or a fly.\n\nSo, the answer is certain, which is option A.\n\n</think>.\n\nThe statement "Rock does not have wings" is uncertain because Rock could be a bird (which has wings) or a fly (where we don\'t know if it has wings). Therefore, my final option is: ']] 70%|######9   | 142/204 [2:56:14<2:34:01, 149.05s/it]
