dying (T).\n4. People who work regularly at home (W) visit the office supply store regularly (V).\n5. If people tidy (T), they do not go to bed late and wake up late (S).\n6. Remy either both goes to bed late and wakes up late (S) and tidies (T), or does neither.\n\n### Logical Variables:\n- M: Owns a large desktop monitor.\n- W: Works regularly at home.\n- H: Has a fully stocked home office.\n- T: Spends free time tidying.\n- V: Visits the office supply store regularly.\n- S: Goes to bed late and wakes up late.\n\n### Key Deductions:\n- From statement 6, Remy is either (S \u2227 T) or (\u00acS \u2227 \u00acT). However, (S \u2227 T) is impossible due to statement 5 (T \u2192 \u00acS), so Remy must be (\u00acS \u2227 \u00acT).\n- Since Remy is \u00acT, from statement 3 (W \u2192 T), Remy is \u00acW.\n- From statement 1 (M \u2192 W), Remy is \u00acM.\n- From statement 2 (H \u2192 M), Remy is \u00acH.\n- From statement 4 (W \u2192 V), since Remy is \u00acW, V could be true or false.\n\n### Statement Evaluation:\nThe statement is: If Remy either goes to bed late (S) or visits the store (V), then Remy neither tidies (\u00acT) nor has a home office (\u00acH).\n\n- Remy is \u00acT and \u00acH, so the conclusion is always true.\n- The antecedent (S \u2228 V) could be true or false, but the conclusion is always true.\n\nThus, the statement is true because the conclusion is always true, regardless of the antecedent.\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\boxed{A}",
