d thus not handsome), Harry could be evil because he\'s not handsome.Therefore, Harry might not be kind.\n\nBut does not being a kind gentleman make him a CEO?The context doesn\'t say that all gentlemen are CEOs, only that all CEOs are gentlemen.So being a gentleman is not a necessary condition for being a CEO.There could be non-gentlemen who are CEOs.\n\nSo, while Harry is not necessarily a gentleman, we don\'t have any information that directly links him to being a CEO.He could be a CEO, but he might not be.There\'s no evidence either way, so we can\'t definitively say he is a CEO.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Harry is a CEO" is uncertain based on the given information.\n\n</think>.\n\nThe statement "Harry is a CEO" is uncertain because while Harry is a gentleman, the context doesn\'t provide enough information to confirm he is a CEO. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
