ue due to the lack of evidence supporting the existence of flu and its impact on people\'s energy levels.\n\nConsidering that the context does not state the presence of flu but rather mentions tiredness as a symptom of glu (flu), it implies that flu is not a real condition and does not cause any symptoms. Therefore, the statement that no one gets flu is true as there is no confirmation of its existence.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be A) True.\n\n</think>.\n\nThe context implies that flu exists as it mentions people feeling tired when they get it. Therefore, the statement "No one gets flu" is false. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
