      "text": " C) Uncertain.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Understanding Premises:**\n   - All mammals are animals.\n   - All monkeys are mammals.\n   - Animals are either monkeys or birds.\n   - All birds fly.\n   - All animals breathe.\n   - If something flies, it has wings.\n   - If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n2. **Analyzing Rock's Possibilities:**\n   - Rock could be a fly or a bird (both have wings).\n   - Rock could be neither, implying it doesn't fly or breathe.\n\n3. **Determining Rock's Nature:**\n   - If Rock is a fly or bird, it has wings.\n   - If Rock is neither, it doesn't fly or breathe, but since all animals breathe, Rock must be an animal, thus a monkey or bird.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Rock's status as a fly or bird is uncertain, making the presence of wings uncertain.\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Final Answer:** C) Uncertain\n\n**Answer:** C) Uncert